**Code for deleting a node in a linked list without access to the head:**

```c
void deleteNode(Node* x) {
    Node* temp = x->next;
    x->data = temp->data;
    x->next = temp->next;
    delete temp;
}
```

This code will delete the next node of `x` and update `x` to point to the next node after that. The deleted node is not kept in memory, so this operation has a time complexity of O(1).

```python
class Solution:
    def solve(self, node):
        if not node or not node.next:
            return

        # Copy the data from the next node to the current node
        node.val = node.next.val
        # Bypass the next node by changing the pointer of the current node to skip the next node
        node.next = node.next.next
```
